message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Marshall Triangle: A Triadic Geometric Framework for Modeling Balance in Complex Systems"
version: v1.1.2
date-released: "2026-07-27"
authors:
  - family-names: Marshall
    given-names: Paul W.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3674-7883"
    affiliation: "Fidelitas LLC"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20696528
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paul-W-Marshall/marshall-triangle"
url: "https://marshalltriangle.app"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  The Marshall Triangle is a formal geometric framework for representing balance
  among three competing system priorities. Inspired by color-space visualization,
  simplex geometry, and multi-objective tradeoff modeling, the framework maps
  triadic states into a continuous triangular domain in which relative dominance,
  pairwise blending, and equilibrium can be explored visually and mathematically.
keywords:
  - triadic modeling
  - computational geometry
  - simplex visualization
  - system balance
  - harmony index
  - visual analytics
  - multi-objective tradeoffs
  - color-space models
  - radial basis functions
